+      "title": "LQG exact metric dimension: the unidentified exponent",
+      "statement": "DRAFT research synthesis, pending w521 review. For 0<gamma<2, let h be a whole-plane GFF and D_h its canonical gamma-LQG metric. The target is the deterministic number d_gamma=dim_H(C,D_h). Set xi=gamma/d_gamma and Q=2/gamma+gamma/2. The median a_epsilon of left-right crossing length in the unit square for heat-kernel-mollified LFPP satisfies a_epsilon=epsilon^(1-xi*Q(xi)+o(1)), and Q(gamma/d_gamma)=Q. The exact function xi -> Q(xi) is the missing input. Scalar scaling, KPZ identities or a subpower change of normalization alone do not evaluate it. The sqrt(8/3) case has d_gamma=4; a primary survey published 13 July 2026 reports general d_gamma as unknown, while current openness on 10 October is not certified by this packet. Sources: Ding-Dubedat-Gwynne arXiv:2109.01252v2 equations (2.3)-(2.5), Problem 5.1; Holden-Sun DOI 10.1137/25M181012X, Section 2.",
