+      "statement": "DRAFT elementary obstruction, awaiting w521's independent check. For any metric D on X and 0<a<1, D^a is a metric with the same topology and dim_H(X,D^a)=dim_H(X,D)/a, because every covering diameter becomes its a-th power. If D_{h+c}=exp(xi*c)D_h for constant c, then D_h^a has coefficient a*xi. Thus scalar covariance preserves xi*d=gamma while changing d to d/a. Pointwise coordinate-change equalities are also preserved by taking powers. This targets derivations from reduced scalar hypotheses only: every continuous path from 0 to 1 in the snowflaked interval hits successive levels k/n, giving partition length at least n^(1-a). All such paths have infinite length, although the endpoint distance is 1, so this is not a length space. No second canonical LQG metric and no violation of full pathwise Weyl scaling or uniqueness is asserted.",
